<Defs>

<!--

Notes:
-Vivium is an alloy with undeterminate amount of silver, gold, and jade. It will always produce a random amount of all three when melted down. 
-All can also be graded or melted down.
-Grading makes the implant unusable, but turns it into art and increases the value considerably.
-Midas-Class Implants don't really give bonuses beyond beauty or social.

To make implants that react to damage, the following comp can be used:
    <comps>
      <li Class="HediffCompProperties_ReactOnDamage">
        <damageDefIncoming>EMP</damageDefIncoming>
        <createHediff>BrainShock</createHediff>
      </li>
    </comps>

Todo:
	-Golden/Silver/Vivium Jaw: a jaw with all teeth of the given material. Gives extra social and beauty.
	-Golden/Silver/Vivium Skull: a skull made out of the full material.
	-Golden/Silver/Vivium Eye. an eye made out of of the given material. No extra sight, but gives extra beauty.
	-Golden/Silver/Vivium Kidney: a kidney made out of the given material.

	-Chronite Kidney: a kidney that increases blood filtration and injury regeneration, but adds an innate pain.
	-Chronite Lung: a lung that increases toxin filtration, but adds an innate pain.
	-Chronite Mech Tether: A brain implant that continuously debuffs mech in range. Affects friendly mechs too. Lowers pawn conciousness and psychic sensitivity.
	-Biothite Slumbergem: A brain implant that lowers rest rate multiplier, but drastically decreases sleep fall rate. Causes innate pain.
	-Deeproot Linkspine: Connects the user to the fungal network below, giving them a 20% conciousness boost and speeds at everything else, but lowering movement speed and also causing random mood swings.
	-Biothite Nerve Dampener: A spine implant that reduces Pain by 90%. No drawbacks, but extremely rare.
	-Deeproot Linkleg: Leg replacements that connect the pawn to the network below, lowing their movement speed but massively increasing carry weight. Also regenerates part health.


Bloomcore Serum: Ancient slave tech that infuses a pawn with hardened skin and glowing purple aspects. Once they die, they explode into a Nightshade explosive that lingers for days, quickly killing anything around it.

Terrameld gets introduced as a basic material that also replaces parts on a pawn. This material specifically uses organic materials, and only goes up to 110% efficiency on any part.

Terrameld prosthetics can first be acquired by placing normal limbs below a Reclaimer Tree.


Terrameld Oculus: A collection of carefully grown, organic bioreceptors that allow the user to see the world. Due to its plant origins, the image one sees with this eye is extremely unique, as it blurs out most of the visual ‘noise’ human-likes would otherwise see every day - which is almost everything. Similarly, anything that would be important to a plant - or in the case, the person - would be in sharp focus as soon as the subconscious registers it.

Due to this it takes a long time to get used to, and many won’t appreciate the lack of detail. However, those who wish to get as close to nature as they can may appreciate - and even envy - this kind of unique perspective.
Final results (per eye):
	-Sight: 30%
	-Not affected by light levels
	-Increase of 0.5 to Plant Skills
	-Increase of 0.3 to Foraged food amounts.
	-Increase of 1 to dodge chances.
	-Negative mood of -5 for anyone that is into higher tech/bionics.
	-Positive mood of +5 for anyone that is into nature/art.

-->

  <!--===== Vivium Jaw =====-->

  <HediffDef ParentName="AddedBodyPartBase">
    <defName>ET_ViviumJaw</defName>
    <label>vivium jaw</label>
    <labelNoun>a vivium jaw</labelNoun>
    <description>An installed vivium jaw. While not as effective as a normal jaw, it's terratech nature makes it better than a denture... and it's alloy materials make any smiles quite radiant.</description>
    <descriptionHyperlinks>
      <ThingDef>ET_ViviumJaw</ThingDef>
    </descriptionHyperlinks>
    <spawnThingOnRemoved>ET_ViviumJaw</spawnThingOnRemoved>
    <addedPartProps>
      <solid>true</solid>
      <partEfficiency>0.9</partEfficiency>
      <betterThanNatural>true</betterThanNatural>
    </addedPartProps>
	<stages>
      <li>
        <statOffsets>
			<TradePriceImprovement>0.1</TradePriceImprovement>
        	<PawnBeauty>1</PawnBeauty>
        </statOffsets>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </HediffDef>

  <ThingDef ParentName="ET_BodyPartLithicBase">
    <defName>ET_ViviumJaw</defName>
    <label>vivium jaw</label>
    <description>A jaw made entirely out of vivium alloy, fitted with a full set of matching teeth. Unlike pure silver and gold, vivium is strong enough to perform the everyday tasks any person would need teeth to do... such as chewing. Still, it is not functionally better than actual bone.</description>
    <descriptionHyperlinks>
      <RecipeDef>ET_InstallViviumJaw</RecipeDef>
    </descriptionHyperlinks>
    <statBases>
      <Mass>1.1</Mass>
    </statBases>
  </ThingDef>

  <RecipeDef ParentName="SurgeryInstallBodyPartArtificialBase">
    <defName>ET_InstallViviumJaw</defName>
    <label>Install vivium jaw</label>
    <description>Install vivium jaw.</description>
    <jobString>Installing vivium jaw.</jobString>
    <ingredients>
      <li>
        <filter>
          <thingDefs>
            <li>ET_ViviumJaw</li>
          </thingDefs>
        </filter>
        <count>1</count>
      </li>
    </ingredients>
    <fixedIngredientFilter>
      <thingDefs>
        <li>ET_ViviumJaw</li>
      </thingDefs>
    </fixedIngredientFilter>
    <appliedOnFixedBodyParts>
      <li>Jaw</li>
    </appliedOnFixedBodyParts>
    <addsHediff>ET_ViviumJaw</addsHediff>
  </RecipeDef>

